{
  "_readme": "Pi RPC uses JSONL envelopes with a top-level type. Extension UI requests also carry a method. These tables keep the Go provider and TypeScript plugin consistent. The role and stop reason tables hold the values that either reader compares. The unread table states each reader exception.\n\nLeapMux supplements retain partial results beside native frames. Native Pi reports fullOutputPath directly in result details. The browser shows that path beside the original preview. Codemode keeps its status header before its output. MCP results keep their native structured content inline. LeapMux reads no output file.\n\nGenerated structs use the same table keys as the decoders. Native result keys and LeapMux supplement keys keep separate ownership. Go-only RPC command names stay in providers/pi/protocol.go. The shared pi_message_content_conformance fixture checks resolution in both languages.",
